==========================================
NETWORKING DAY 15 — PROJECT 2
Capture Your Lab Traffic, Write a Short Report
==========================================

--- SETUP ---
python3 -m http.server 8080              # Terminal 1: local web server on your own machine
ip route                                  # find your gateway (address after "default via")

--- CAPTURE WITH TCPDUMP (needs sudo; stop with Ctrl+C) ---
sudo tcpdump -i lo -n 'tcp port 8080' -w web.pcap        # web traffic on loopback
sudo tcpdump -i eth0 -n 'icmp or port 53' -w net.pcap      # ping + DNS on your real interface
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/ > /dev/null                   # generate a request (run it 3 times)
ping -c 4 <gateway-ip>                                         # generate ICMP
dig example.com                                                  # generate a DNS lookup
ls -lh *.pcap                                                     # sizes of the capture files

--- READ A CAPTURE BACK (no sudo needed) ---
tcpdump -r web.pcap -n | head -20                                  # first packets
tcpdump -r web.pcap -n 'tcp[tcpflags] & tcp-syn != 0'               # only SYN and SYN-ACK packets
tcpdump -r net.pcap -n                                                # everything in the ping/DNS capture

--- FACT EXTRACTION WITH TSHARK ---
capinfos web.pcap                                                      # packets, duration, file size
tshark -r web.pcap -q -z conv,tcp                                       # TCP conversation table
tshark -r web.pcap -Y http -T fields -e http.user_agent -e http.server    # client tool + server software
tshark -r web.pcap -Y http.response -T fields -e http.time                  # server response time per request
tshark -r net.pcap -Y "dns.flags.response == 1" -T fields -e dns.qry.name -e dns.a -e dns.time
tshark -r net.pcap -Y "icmp.type == 0" -T fields -e icmp.resptime             # ping round trips (replies)
   # if a field prints nothing, open the same file in Wireshark and read it from the packet details pane

--- WRITING THE REPORT ---
cp REPORT_TEMPLATE.md report.md                                         # start from the template
every finding -> name the command or screenshot that proves it
limits section -> say what you did NOT capture

--- RULES TO KEEP ---
Capture only on your own machine and your own lab network.
Stop captures as soon as the traffic you care about is done.
Use a capture filter so unrelated traffic doesn't fill the file.

